      "measure": "lighthouse",
      "metrics": "web.lab.lcp.max{device=mobile} <= baseline + {{LAB_MARGIN}}%\nweb.lab.cls.max{device=mobile} <= baseline + {{LAB_MARGIN}}%\nweb.lab.tbt.max{device=mobile} <= baseline + {{LAB_MARGIN}}%",
      "description": "For a front end that starts above the budget: every pull request runs Lighthouse's mobile default (a mid-range phone on a slow 4G connection, simulated) three times on each main page and radical sense lighthouse reads the medians; each value may be at most {{LAB_MARGIN}}% worse than the main branch's. The job on main keeps its reports/metrics file as an artifact, and the pull request's job passes the latest seven to radical check with --baseline, which compares with their median. Both run on runners of one class, so the speed of the machine cancels out. lighthouserc.cjs holds no assertions: the conditions are the model's. When the pages are within the budget ({{LCP_MS}} ms LCP, {{CLS}} CLS, {{TBT_MS}} ms TBT), answer the lab question again with fixed limits.\n\nThreshold: For the slowest main page, median of three runs with Lighthouse's mobile default (a mid-range phone on a slow 4G connection, simulated): LCP, CLS and Total Blocking Time each at most {{LAB_MARGIN}}% above the median of the main branch's latest seven runs\n\nTool: Lighthouse CI (@lhci/cli) with radical sense lighthouse\n\n```js\n// lighthouserc.cjs: Lighthouse CI only collects; the model's conditions judge the numbers\nmodule.exports = {\n  ci: {\n    collect: {\n      startServerCommand: 'npm run preview',\n      url: ['http://localhost:4173/', 'http://localhost:4173/search', 'http://localhost:4173/checkout'],\n      numberOfRuns: 3,\n      // puppeteerScript: './lighthouse-login.cjs',   // signs in first, for pages behind sign-in\n    },\n  },\n}\n// The pull-request job (no assert, no upload: radical check fails the job):\n//   npx @lhci/cli@0.15.1 collect                                        # phones: Lighthouse's mobile default\n//   npx @lhci/cli@0.15.1 collect --additive --settings.preset=desktop   # desktops; without --additive when only desktops count\n//   npx radical sense run --trigger pull-request --out reports/metrics  # lighthouse reads .lighthouseci, machine times the runner\n//   npx radical check --metrics reports/metrics\n```",
      "hubWhen": {
        "DEVICES": [
          "mobile",
          "both"
        ],
        "LAB": [
          "baseline"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ff-lab-desktop-trend",
